"]],["p-2c7f72fa22286f63.html","source-block-1712","GitP/A/Session/24/11/19-Tue/Asset/Synth/Full/mp3",["Updated","gitpa"]],["p-2c7f72fa22286f63.html","source-block-1769","GitP/A/Session/24/12/04-Wed/Asset/Artwork/Overview/gif",["Updated","gitpa"]],["p-2c7f72fa22286f63.html","source-block-1832","GitP/A/Session/24/12/04-Wed/Asset/MIDI/Microfreak/mid",["Updated","gitpa"]],["p-2c7f72fa22286f63.html","source-block-1894","GitP/A/Session/24/12/04-Wed/Asset/Preset/A/mfpz",["Updated","gitpa"]],["p-2c7f72fa22286f63.html","source-block-1950","GitP/A/Session/24/12/04-Wed/Asset/Preset/B/mfpz",["Updated","gitpa"]],["p-2c7f72fa22286f63.html","source-block-2006","GitP/A/Session/24/12/04-Wed/Asset/Preset/C/mfpz",["Updated","gitpa"]],["p-2c7f72fa22286f63.html","source-block-2062","GitP/A/Session/24/12/04-Wed/Asset/Preset/D/mfpz",["Updated","gitpa"]],["p-2c7f72fa22286f63.html","source-block-2118","GitP/A/Session/24/12/04-Wed/Asset/Synth/Full/mp3",["Updated","gitpa"]],["p-2c7f72fa22286f63.html","source-block-2175","GitP/A/Session/26/09/25-Fri/Asset/Synth/Full/mp3",["Updated","gitpa"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-0","My Thoughts",[]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-18","Working with AI feels a little like assembling Zonai devices in a Zelda game: you have to build the machine that will go do the thing.",["My Thoughts"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-156","Selective skill activation",["My Thoughts"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-189","This morning I was reviewing a pr my agents opened in my dotfiles to install TWG/Agent/Skills, which would make the skill available globally, much like the global skills that ship with herdr.",["My Thoughts","Selective skill activation"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-442","I installed herdr a while back, used it heavily for a week, and haven't touched it sense, mostly because its conceptual model was rough.",["My Thoughts","Selective skill activation"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-587","I still want to keep it around in my arsenal in case it develops into a more agent native mental model that I can understand and that works with my workflows. For example, if it had task awareness, with task-worker mapping, hierarchical agents, honoring worktrees within projects, and allowing one to switch between projects quickly like the tmux Session Picker, that would be great.",["My Thoughts","Selective skill activation","I installed herdr a while back, used it heavily for a week, and haven't touched it sense, mostly because its conceptual model was rough."]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-980","Yesterday, I noticed that something in my My/Dotfiles installed, with herdr, an AI/Agent/Hook that loads context on session load. That's pretty inefficient! That means that all my sessions - even those that don't begin in herdr - get that loaded in. I need to fix that.",["My Thoughts","Selective skill activation"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-1266","Ghost Gardener please investigate this and file a github issue",["My Thoughts","Selective skill activation","Yesterday, I noticed that something in my My/Dotfiles installed, with herdr, an AI/Agent/Hook that loads context on session load. That's pretty inefficient! Tha"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-1343","codekiln/dotfiles#144 herdr skill loads in every agent session: the global rulesync install puts the herdr skill in sessions without HERDR_ENV; no hook is involved.",["Selective skill activation","Yesterday, I noticed that something in my My/Dotfiles installed, with herdr, an AI/Agent/Hook that loads context on session load. That's pretty inefficient! Tha","Ghost Gardener please investigate this and file a github issue"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-1567","Better mechanisms",["My Thoughts","Selective skill activation"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-1593","Ideally, I'd have some kind of settings that I could edit from the terminal that, either globally or in a particular session, would specify the workflows I expect my agents to use. Then I could easily activate or deactivate the plugins and skills that I think should be active.",["My Thoughts","Selective skill activation","Better mechanisms"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-1876","2026-10-05 Mon I added the workspace to record a few of these workflows. Maybe I could list which ones were active globally there as a default, then somehow I could indicate on a task-specific basis which workflows should deviate from those defaults.",["My Thoughts","Selective skill activation","Better mechanisms"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-2164","Added Idea/Fortui - the Form TUI Markup Language.",["My Thoughts","Selective skill activation","Better mechanisms"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-2223","Most of this is only relevant in a world where context is limited.",["My Thoughts","Selective skill activation"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-2294","Standards for the , Principles, The , the of a project Goals, Product Vision as well as the how of the",["My Thoughts"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-2490","Idea/Standard/Project/Management/Schema",["My Thoughts","Standards for the , Principles, The , the of a project Goals, Product Vision as well as the how of the"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-2538","Idea/Standard/Project/Vision and Goals",["My Thoughts","Standards for the , Principles, The , the of a project Goals, Product Vision as well as the how of the"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-2599","atlassian",[]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-2612","TWG/Agent/Skill",["atlassian"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-2636","gitpa",[]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-2645","GitP/A/Log/26/10/06 Tue - gitpa proxy follow-ups",["gitpa"]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-2702","ideas",[]],["p-fe269b8defaa7d22.html","source-block-2711","Idea/Fortui - the Form TUI Markup Language",["ideas"]],["p-fe269b